# Logging

## Winston Only

- Use `logger` from `@seller/shared` for all logging
- **No** `console.log`, `console.error`, `console.warn`, `console.debug` — banned in backend code

## Usage

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
import { logger } from '@seller/shared';

logger.info('Message');
logger.error('Failed', error);
logger.warn('Deprecated', { id });
logger.debug('Debug data', obj);
```

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
console.log('message');
console.error('error', err);
```

## NestJS API

- Inject `LoggerService` in services/controllers for Nest-aware context
- Nest bootstrap uses it automatically; internal Nest logs go through Winston too
